          "_key": "24eb51946feb",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Why GRE Is Important for Studying Abroad"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h4"
    },
    {
      "_key": "4d700e7ea6b4",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "f94c478c827d",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "If you are planning to pursue higher education abroad, then understanding the "
        },
        {
          "_key": "9a5690f5fc49",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "GRE for study abroad"
        },
        {
          "_key": "a83613e27d5c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " is essential. The Graduate Record Examination (GRE) is widely accepted by universities across the globe. Therefore, a good GRE score can significantly improve your chances of admission to top international institutions."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "236dc6c385cd",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "af6698bad61a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Moreover, many universities use GRE scores to assess analytical thinking, quantitative ability, and verbal reasoning skills. As a result, students with strong GRE performance often stand out during the admission process. At "
        },
        {
          "_key": "5807ecb28291",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Admizz Education"
        },
        {
          "_key": "389281beba55",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", we guide students step by step—from GRE preparation to final university admission."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "e72360389108",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "7378667d10fa",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What Is the GRE Exam?"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h4"
    },
    {
      "_key": "5f8c97214946",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "9faaac9f32d7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The "
        },
        {
          "_key": "4b3aa9164644",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "GRE"
        },
        {
          "_key": "fb2d1610145d",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", conducted by "
        },
        {
          "_key": "1ea599d3c92c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "ETS (Educational Testing Service)"
        },
        {
          "_key": "bad15ca248a4",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", is a standardized test required for admission into various graduate and doctoral programs. While some universities have made GRE optional, many top-ranked institutions still prefer or recommend it."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "9dea34525214",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "f80867d7490c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Additionally, GRE scores are accepted across multiple countries, making the exam highly flexible for international applicants."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "a3db6ab07883",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
